    "text": "To determine how many kids are still awake, we will follow the steps outlined in the problem:\n\n1. **Initial number of kids**: There are 20 kids in preschool.\n\n2. **Kids who fall asleep in the first 5 minutes**: \n   - Half of the kids fall asleep within the first 5 minutes.\n   - Number of kids who fall asleep: \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 = 10 \\)\n   - Number of kids still awake: \\( 20 - 10 = 10 \\)\n\n3. **Kids who fall asleep in the next 5 minutes**: \n   - Half of the remaining kids fall asleep within the next 5 minutes.\n   - Number of kids remaining: 10\n   - Number of kids who fall asleep: \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 = 5 \\)\n   - Number of kids still awake: \\( 10 - 5 = 5 \\)\n\nThus, the number of kids still awake is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
